## Antigravity-specific

- **Commit attribution:** `Co-Authored-By: Antigravity <noreply@anthropic.com>` — this is the one
  place the `AGENTS.md` attribution rule is specialized by vendor.
- **One packet per turn.** Complete it fully: edit → verify gate → commit. Do not open a second
  unit of work in the same turn.
- **Re-anchor before editing.** Any `file:line` reference you were handed may have moved; grep for
  the symbol first. If the symbol is gone, stop and report rather than guessing.
- **IDE leverage** (this is an editor, not a CLI — use it): resolve Error Lens warnings inline
  before running verify gates; check GitLens blame before modifying code in a concurrent-worktree
  session; validate `schema.prisma` with the Prisma extension before generating the client; keep
  `.http` playbooks under `docs/operations/` rather than reaching for an external client.
- **Machine-local tooling is not repo truth.** Local MCP servers, Ollama models and IDE extensions
  exist on this laptop only — verify availability before depending on one, and never encode a
  local-machine assumption into repo code or CI.
